{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>But this is a people plundered.</b> It takes a heh [as object marker], like שׁוֹסִי׳ אֶת הַגֳּרָנוֹת (1 Samuel 23:1)." "<b>Trap.</b> A noun of action, like נְפִיחָה; and if they are two roots." "<b>In holes.</b> From the root of חֹר פָּתֶן (Isaiah 11:8), and the meaning is that they are bound, sitting at the bottom of those who went out from captivity." "<b>Restore.</b> With the vav that is at the end of a verse, and it is a transitive verb: he restores [the one] who took captive." "<b>Who among you will declare this.</b> Like this prophet, about whom you say that he is blind. The future [tense] is heard [used] with retrospective force, and this is from the root of אַל תְּאַחֲרוּ אֹתִי (Genesis 24:56)." "<b>Former things.</b> From the root of פנה."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:40.781149607Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}